From 41dda235b89a4e0fb543d76c96eadeb57f120fe8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:19:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] samsung_securefp: add a driver for Samsung's TrustZone
 fingerprint TA

On Samsung phones the fingerprint sensor belongs to the secure world:
Samsung's "securefp" trusted application owns the SPI bus, captures,
extracts and matches, and returns opaque sealed templates. The normal
world only loads the TA, powers the sensor, pulses its reset line and
waits on its interrupt line whenever the TA asks for it, which is what
Samsung's Android HAL (libbauthserver) does.

The driver does the same through the kernel's /dev/qsee-app interface,
found through the misc udev subtype. Each TA command is repeated with the
HAL's "op" word until the TA reports it done; in between, the driver
serves the TA's requests (wait for the interrupt, sleep, reset). A finger
wait that times out is not a failure: as in the HAL, the command is
called again and the TA decides. The interrupt and reset lines are found
by their DT line names, power is the "fingerprint-power" regulator-output,
and the board (TA path, sensor type) comes from a table keyed by the DT
compatible. Templates are stored by fprintd inside the FpPrint.

The session follows the HAL. A cold open powers the sensor (rail off,
then on, then reset high, 11 ms apart, as the stock kernel driver does)
and loads the TA. The first operation runs Prepare with the calibration
the TA handed out last time, kept in /var/lib/samsung-securefp/calib.dat:
op 1 with the blob, or op 2 (first call) without one or when the TA
cannot open it (status 0x1c). Without its calibration the TA measures a
new sensor base on every Prepare, also with a finger on the sensor; with
it, it only does so when the finger is up. Later operations on the open
session skip Prepare and go straight to their Init. Closing the device
keeps the session for 10 s, so a lock screen that restarts its PAM
conversation finds it warm; then the driver sends the HAL's cleanup
control op, keeps the calibration it returns, unloads the TA and powers
the sensor off.

Operations run in a worker thread; progress and finger status are posted
back to the device's main context.

Supported so far: Galaxy Z Flip3 (samsung,b2q, Goodix GW36T1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
